Patch against guybedford/workers-rs @ emscripten root Cargo.toml.

Detaches the unrelated `emscripten-goose` example (a clipboard/tree-sitter/sys-info
demo the QUIC crates don't touch) from the workspace. This is REQUIRED, not cosmetic:
goose's `tree-sitter` submodule points at `github.com/guybedford/tree-sitter`, which
no longer exists ("Repository not found"), so its `tree-sitter.path` dependency can
never resolve — a full-workspace resolve is impossible while goose is a member.

Both hunks are load-bearing:
  1. Exclude `examples/emscripten-goose` from the workspace members.
  2. Drop the goose-only `[workspace.dependencies]` (arboard/fs2/sys-info/tree-sitter).
     cargo *eagerly* loads workspace.dependency path sources even when unused, so
     leaving them fails on the missing `./arboard` etc.; and goose inherits them via
     `.workspace = true`, so it needs excluding once they're gone.

(quinn-udp is NOT patched: its portable `unix.rs` compiles unmodified once the
emscripten `libc` gains `in6_pktinfo` — see patches/libc-emscripten-in6_pktinfo.patch.)

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index 9a6a1d9..8e2df5b 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@ members = [
 exclude = [
     "examples/coredump",
     "examples/axum",
+    "examples/emscripten-goose",
     "templates/*",
     "wasm-bindgen",
     "wasm-streams",
@@ -119,17 +120,15 @@ wasm-bindgen-macro-support = { version = "0.2.121", path = "./wasm-bindgen/crate
 wasm-bindgen-shared = { version = "0.2.121", path = "./wasm-bindgen/crates/shared" }
 wasm-bindgen-test = { version = "0.3.71", path = "./wasm-bindgen/crates/test" }
 web-sys = { version = "0.3.98", path = './wasm-bindgen/crates/web-sys' }
-arboard.path = "./arboard"
-fs2.path = "./fs2-rs"
 libc.path = "./libc"
 socket2.git = "https://github.com/rust-lang/socket2"
-sys-info.path = "./sys-info"
 ring.path = "./ring"
 tokio-macros.path = "./tokio/tokio-macros"
 tokio.path = "./tokio/tokio"
-# Emscripten has a full libc, so tree-sitter must not compile its libc-less
-# wasm shims (stdio/stdlib/...) — they duplicate `fwrite` et al. The local
-# `tree-sitter` submodule (emscripten branch, v0.26.9 base — matching goose's
-# req.) carries that build.rs fix.
-tree-sitter.path = "./tree-sitter/lib"
-tree-sitter-language.path = "./tree-sitter/crates/language"
+# --- goose-only patches (arboard/fs2/sys-info/tree-sitter) disabled for the
+# --- QUIC POC; emscripten-goose is excluded from the workspace above.
+# arboard.path = "./arboard"
+# fs2.path = "./fs2-rs"
+# sys-info.path = "./sys-info"
+# tree-sitter.path = "./tree-sitter/lib"
+# tree-sitter-language.path = "./tree-sitter/crates/language"
